.agent/active/reviews/p5_2_review_retry.log:2001:.agent/active/v1.2.0_execplan_rev1.md:95:**統合判断:** **Plan B's pattern wins.** Reading the credential from a path (not from an env-var that's visible to `systemctl show`) raises the security floor and matches systemd ≥ 252 idiom exactly. Plan A's "native read of `$CREDENTIALS_DIRECTORY`" is the same idea but Plan B's `..._FILE` env-var pattern is the canonical systemd recipe and requires *zero* rev-auth code changes (only a 5-line keystore.rs addition that reads `$REV_SCRAPING_AUTH_PASSPHRASE_FILE` if set). Document env-only fallback for distros < systemd 252.
